<title>UK: Mexico's Pemex widens some Jan crude discounts.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex widens some Jan crude discounts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state-owned oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) widened the discounts against it's pricing formulae of the following crudes for export in January.</p>
<p>Discounts to the formulae for Isthmus crude to the Americas widened by 10 cents to -$1, while Maya crudes to the Far East and Europe wre marked 30 and 25 cents lower at -$3.20 and -$1.75 respectively.</p>
<p>All other differentials were unchanged from December levels.</p>
<p>-- Colin Wooster, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7456</p>
</text>
